# The pipeline's CSVs are written UTF-8-with-BOM + CRLF for Excel (see
# README.md, "Editing the CSV in Excel"). Mark the committed one binary-ish so
# core.autocrlf on a Windows checkout cannot rewrite its line endings out from
# under the byte-comparison in tests/test_oxygen_sample.py.
demo/oxygen-sample/sample.csv -text

# The committed miniature publication is generated output that
# tests/test_oxygen_sample.py byte-compares against a fresh run. The generator
# always writes LF, so a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true turned every
# text file in the tree (topics, ditamaps, ditavals, rewritten .glc configs) to
# CRLF and failed the comparison for 24 files nobody had changed.
demo/oxygen-sample/dita/** -text
